Time Complexity:

Let n = size of array

    Single traversal → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity:

    Only constant variables used

Overall: O(1)


Approach:

1. Initialize flag = 0
   - It stores count of order breaks

2. Traverse array from index 0 to n-2:

   - If nums[i] > nums[i+1]
     → increment flag

3. Analyze break count:

   - If flag > 1:
     → array cannot be sorted and rotated
     → return false

   - If flag == 1:
     → check if first element ≥ last element
     → return result

   - If flag == 0:
     → array is already sorted
     → return true



class Solution {
    public boolean check(int[] nums) {
        int flag=0;
        for(int i=0; i<nums.length-1; i++){
            if(nums[i]>nums[i+1]) flag++;
        }
        if(flag==1) return nums[0]>=nums[nums.length-1];
        if(flag>1) return false;
        return true;
    }
}
